media: sun50i-h713-hdmirx: video range and picture mode as controls, converter state in status

Two firmware settings that the picture depends on were reachable only
through the debugfs RPC prompt: THal_Vp_SetVideoRange and
THal_Vp_SetPictureMode. Give them the same shape as the nine picture
controls of 0101 -- one control, one RPC, the bring-up value as the
default. Video Range is a menu (Auto, Limited, Full: 0, 1, 2 as the
firmware counts them); Picture Mode is an integer 0..7, because the
vendor's ini names eight modes but which number is which has not been
measured, and a menu with guessed names would be a claim.

The converter restore of 0123 used to toggle full range and back to auto.
With a range control that would silently reset a user's choice on every
resolution change; now it steps away from the chosen value and back to it.

The status file gains the two lines this session kept reading by hand:
the capture enable (0x928 bit 31) and the input converter (0x824 bit 31,
BYPASS is the green picture). The board has no v4l2-ctl; this is where a
userspace tool looks.

